1
00:02:04,816 --> 00:02:06,816


2
00:02:19,270 --> 00:02:20,760
Where am I?

3
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:25,940
Babies about to be born are being sent down to Earth.

4
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:27,660
That's it!

5
00:02:27,995 --> 00:02:29,260
This is Heaven!

6
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:32,520
I must be dreaming of Heaven.

7
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:34,540
This is me!

8
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:50,000
Back when I was in Heaven, I was quite a mischievous angel.

9
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:04,460
God is separating the babies into boys and girls!

10
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,980
There, open wide!

11
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:13,180
The child who drinks the blue heart becomes a boy, and the child who drinks the red heart becomes a girl!

12
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,760
There, open wide!

13
00:03:15,861 --> 00:03:18,580
I stole a blue heart from the basket!

14
00:03:19,721 --> 00:03:21,660
Hey, wouldn't it be better to be a boy?

15
00:03:21,970 --> 00:03:23,680
I don't know which is better.

16
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,920
I'll give you a boy's heart.

17
00:03:27,754 --> 00:03:29,040
Who's next?

18
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:33,000
You are going to be a girl.

19
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:35,180
The child who swallows the red heart will become a girl!

20
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:37,160
I already swallowed the blue heart.

21
00:03:38,235 --> 00:03:40,060
So it's Tink's doing again!

22
00:03:40,235 --> 00:03:41,780
Where is that Tink hiding?

23
00:03:42,424 --> 00:03:43,424
Right there!

24
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:45,575
I'm sorry.

25
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,840
Apologizing won't fix this!

26
00:03:47,045 --> 00:03:51,020
When that child is born, won't it be impossible to tell if it's a boy or a girl?

27
00:03:51,225 --> 00:03:54,120
Go down to the mortal realm and extract the boy's heart from that child!

28
00:03:54,414 --> 00:03:55,414
Do you understand?

29
00:03:56,326 --> 00:03:57,120
Go!

30
00:04:02,664 --> 00:04:05,260
What, so it was just a dream after all?

31
00:04:49,413 --> 00:04:50,080
Tink!

32
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:52,480
Tink!

33
00:04:53,110 --> 00:04:55,540
Ugh, shut up already...

34
00:04:57,710 --> 00:05:00,440
A-a-a-choo!

35
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:02,500
Who is it?

36
00:05:02,550 --> 00:05:04,520
Calling me in the middle of the night like this.

37
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:05,700
It's me.

38
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:08,060
Whoa!

39
00:05:08,070 --> 00:05:09,070
Pegasus!

40
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:10,993
Long time no see.

41
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,859
When did you get here? From Heaven.

42
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,260
What did you come here for?

43
00:05:14,715 --> 00:05:16,233
Hey, how is God doing?

44
00:05:16,790 --> 00:05:19,031
Hey, what's wrong? Pegasus...

45
00:05:19,056 --> 00:05:22,400
Tink, did you forget God's orders?

46
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,500
I can no longer rely on you.

47
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:27,200
I will take Sapphire's boy's heart and return.

48
00:05:27,224 --> 00:05:29,140
Hey, wait up, Pegasus!

49
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:31,440
There's a reason for this, a reason!

50
00:05:31,850 --> 00:05:33,640
Even I know the reason.

51
00:05:34,335 --> 00:05:36,640
When you're in Heaven, you know everything that happens on Earth.

52
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:39,780
But God's command is a command.

53
00:05:40,466 --> 00:05:44,166
I'll do this job myself. Tink, I won't ask you anymore.

54
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:46,027
Hey, don't say that...

55
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:09,226
Ah, I wonder where Pegasus went?

56
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:12,967
At times like this, if I had wings like back when I was in Heaven,

57
00:06:12,991 --> 00:06:15,920
I could float softly through the air like the wind...

58
00:06:18,350 --> 00:06:21,221
Being human is so inconvenient...

59
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,820
Oh no, this is a total disaster!

60
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,680
Pegasus... Your Majesty, I have news!

61
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:56,520
What is it?

62
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:57,660
It's incredible!

63
00:06:57,820 --> 00:07:00,260
The Pegasus... the soaring Pegasus is... What did you say?

64
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,420
A Pegasus?

65
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:03,400
It took flight...

66
00:07:07,180 --> 00:07:08,410
It flew up into the heavens...

67
00:07:14,770 --> 00:07:16,040
It really is a Pegasus.

68
00:07:16,350 --> 00:07:17,660
How wonderful!

69
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:18,920
Truly magnificent.

70
00:07:19,465 --> 00:07:22,368
Happiness will surely come to Silverland...

71
00:07:22,393 --> 00:07:24,841
Yes, it surely will come, happiness...

72
00:07:24,865 --> 00:07:25,466
Why?

73
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:28,160
Hey, why does happiness come when a Pegasus flies?

74
00:07:28,275 --> 00:07:29,960
That's what people have said since ancient times.

75
00:07:30,505 --> 00:07:32,680
I hope the Pegasus stays with us forever.

76
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:40,200
Yeah, is that so... Ah, the Pegasus is going away!

77
00:07:40,445 --> 00:07:42,020
Happiness is slipping away!

78
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,600
Sapphire!

79
00:08:08,345 --> 00:08:09,780
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

80
00:08:11,579 --> 00:08:12,919
Tink, help me.

81
00:08:13,110 --> 00:08:15,480
They say that if you catch that pegasus, happiness will come.

82
00:08:16,174 --> 00:08:17,174
Happiness?

83
00:08:17,305 --> 00:08:20,300
Like I said, that pegasus—there's that kind of legend about it.

84
00:08:20,735 --> 00:08:24,520
I told you, that pegasus didn't bring happiness.

85
00:08:24,825 --> 00:08:28,760
I can't tell you the reason, but it came to make Sapphire more feminine.

86
00:08:40,675 --> 00:08:44,045
A pegasus that brings happiness, huh? I've found something good here.

87
00:10:00,249 --> 00:10:02,424
I was sure it was around here, but...

88
00:10:02,448 --> 00:10:05,115
Well, if it isn't here, it isn't here, Sapphire!

89
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:05,733
Shut up!

90
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:07,380
Tink, wait right there!

91
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:08,780
Got it?

92
00:10:08,809 --> 00:10:10,840
Where could that pegasus have hidden?

93
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:12,359
There it is!

94
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,753
I won't let you get away this time!

95
00:10:16,499 --> 00:10:19,000
Sapphire, you're finally alone.

96
00:10:19,155 --> 00:10:20,400
Ready...

97
00:10:27,339 --> 00:10:28,813
Hey, who did this?

98
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:31,220
I was so close to catching the pegasus, too.

99
00:10:41,189 --> 00:10:44,020
Strange, I thought it was around here...

100
00:10:48,059 --> 00:10:48,920
Nylon!

101
00:10:49,020 --> 00:10:51,213
Well, well, if it isn't Prince Sapphire.

102
00:10:51,395 --> 00:10:52,548
Have you seen a pegasus?

103
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:53,960
A pegasus?

104
00:10:54,164 --> 00:10:55,360
Did you say Pegasus?

105
00:10:55,865 --> 00:10:56,865
It is the horse of happiness.

106
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:58,893
A horse that brings peace to Silverland.

107
00:10:59,714 --> 00:11:00,500
Do you really not know?

108
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:02,240
No, not at all.

109
00:11:02,450 --> 00:11:06,946
Well, that sounds fine, but if such a horse exists, Silverland would be overjoyed.

110
00:11:06,971 --> 00:11:08,880
Now, if you will excuse me.

111
00:11:15,969 --> 00:11:18,180
Fine, my foot! That little tomboy...

112
00:11:19,045 --> 00:11:22,120
The Pegasus is properly loaded in this carriage, you know.

113
00:11:23,145 --> 00:11:25,480
Ah, that's right, I have a good idea. Oh?

114
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:43,300
My, as expected of Grand Duke Duralumin's trick mansion.

115
00:11:49,549 --> 00:11:53,586
The power of the dynamite given by the Grand Duke is truly something.

116
00:11:56,109 --> 00:11:58,505
This is an extraordinarily splendid horse.

117
00:11:58,529 --> 00:12:01,060
But, does having a Pegasus really bring happiness?

118
00:12:01,305 --> 00:12:03,220
Why, yes, yes, of course.

119
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:07,893
What happiness?

120
00:12:08,035 --> 00:12:10,620
Does happiness bite you on the nose, you fool?

121
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:12,660
Please wait, Grand Duke Duralumin.

122
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:16,200
I've thought of something even better. Let me whisper in your ear...

123
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:20,060
Sapphire is?

124
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:22,640
Yes, she is frantically chasing after the Pegasus.

125
00:12:23,239 --> 00:12:26,768
We can use that to finish off that prince once and for all...

126
00:12:26,792 --> 00:12:30,666
Good! Well, aren't you quite the clever one.

127
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:33,500
This is all thanks to bringing the Pegasus...

128
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:47,565
Now then, a horse that looks like a Pegasus... a horse that looks like a Pegasus...

129
00:12:47,589 --> 00:12:49,440
No good, your face is too round.

130
00:12:50,679 --> 00:12:51,980
You've got a mean look in your eyes.

131
00:12:52,005 --> 00:12:54,200
After all, elegance is number one when it comes to being a Pegasus.

132
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:55,780
It must be refined.

133
00:13:09,569 --> 00:13:10,920
Your Grace, it is finished.

134
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,040
How do you like my handiwork?

135
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:13,200
Splendid, splendid.

136
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,540
Just as expected of Nylon.

137
00:13:14,889 --> 00:13:17,460
And now, put this bee inside the fake Pegasus's ear.

138
00:13:17,485 --> 00:13:18,620
The anesthesia lasts for 10 minutes.

139
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:20,420
In 10 minutes, the bee will wake up.

140
00:13:20,705 --> 00:13:24,040
And once the bee goes wild, Sapphire will fall from the top of the tower...

141
00:14:07,219 --> 00:14:08,820
I wonder where the Pegasus went?

142
00:14:08,845 --> 00:14:10,400
Ah, it's over by that door.

143
00:14:11,659 --> 00:14:13,080
Sapphire! Wait!

144
00:14:14,964 --> 00:14:15,797
That's

145
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:16,800
Sapphire!

146
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:17,920
No it's not!!

147
00:14:17,921 --> 00:14:20,360
That's a fake Pegasus!!

148
00:14:21,281 --> 00:14:22,740
I caught you!!

149
00:14:22,741 --> 00:14:26,440
It's about time the fake Pegasus starts going wild, isn't it?!

150
00:14:26,441 --> 00:14:27,480
Come on, fly!!

151
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:28,480
Try flying!!!

152
00:14:28,530 --> 00:14:30,080
Three, two, one, zero!!

153
00:14:30,081 --> 00:14:31,081
Kaboom!!

154
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:32,860
Hey!

155
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:34,420
What's going on?!

156
00:14:34,421 --> 00:14:35,421
Hey!

157
00:14:39,541 --> 00:14:39,840
Hey!

158
00:14:40,185 --> 00:14:41,900
Don't thrash around so much!!

159
00:14:51,606 --> 00:14:53,976
This is terrible, this is terrible, this is terrible!

160
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,579
 Um, I'm in real trouble... Um, um, what should I do? Hey, hey...
Hey, pull yourself together! *Sigh* ...

161
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:58,073
Hey, don't thrash around!

162
00:15:02,030 --> 00:15:02,750
Opal!

163
00:15:05,956 --> 00:15:08,436
Whoa, we're gonna fall!

164
00:15:15,998 --> 00:15:17,045
Oh God!

165
00:15:19,483 --> 00:15:20,817
Thank goodness...

166
00:15:21,979 --> 00:15:23,205
Sapphire!

167
00:15:23,819 --> 00:15:25,393
Sapphire, are you okay?

168
00:15:29,399 --> 00:15:30,977
This was the trick.

169
00:15:31,001 --> 00:15:33,680
They were planning to kill Sapphire from the very beginning, I'm sure of it.

170
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:36,526
Just as I said, it was a fake Pegasus, right?

171
00:15:37,039 --> 00:15:40,330
But who would use a fake Pegasus...?

172
00:15:40,354 --> 00:15:42,740
It's definitely that Nylon guy's doing again.

173
00:15:46,625 --> 00:15:48,980
Ugh, that utterly infuriating Sapphire.

174
00:15:49,090 --> 00:15:51,680
Damn it, just how lucky can that fellow get? Crap!

175
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:53,840
Nylon!

176
00:15:54,639 --> 00:15:55,800
What are you doing in a place like this?

177
00:15:55,935 --> 00:15:59,340
Well, well, Prince Sapphire, I am taking an afternoon stroll.

178
00:15:59,902 --> 00:16:01,053
Now then, if you will excuse me.

179
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:03,020
Wait!

180
00:16:04,769 --> 00:16:06,580
Why did you use a fake Pegasus?

181
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:08,040
Where is the real Pegasus?

182
00:16:09,155 --> 00:16:10,155
What are you talking about?

183
00:16:10,185 --> 00:16:12,620
Your Highness, you seem to be mistaken about something...

184
00:16:12,644 --> 00:16:13,781
Playing dumb won't work!

185
00:16:14,870 --> 00:16:16,140
You're the one who hid the Pegasus.

186
00:16:16,465 --> 00:16:17,680
It has to be right here!

187
00:16:18,209 --> 00:16:21,406
If you insist that much, please, go right ahead and search.

188
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,440
That's enough!

189
00:16:41,655 --> 00:16:45,953
But no matter where you hide it, I will definitely find Pegasus!

190
00:16:53,979 --> 00:16:56,220
Opal, do me a favor.

191
00:16:57,619 --> 00:17:00,120
With your sense of smell, you can tell where Pegasus is, right?

192
00:17:00,745 --> 00:17:01,745
Go search for him.

193
00:17:36,148 --> 00:17:37,608
There's no mistake this time.

194
00:17:37,632 --> 00:17:38,419
 Leave it to me.

195
00:17:38,444 --> 00:17:41,480
I have already set the second and third schemes in motion.

196
00:17:41,875 --> 00:17:44,480
Using this real Pegasus.

197
00:17:50,009 --> 00:17:51,320
Prince Sapphire.

198
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:53,940
Who's there?

199
00:17:54,279 --> 00:17:55,880
I am a humble person.

200
00:17:56,110 --> 00:17:57,680
I have come to bring you news.

201
00:17:57,889 --> 00:18:02,300
Up ahead at the rocky mountain, a Pegasus has its foot trapped between the rocks.

202
00:18:03,419 --> 00:18:04,640
Trapped in the rocks?

203
00:18:05,064 --> 00:18:06,180
Is that true?

204
00:18:22,229 --> 00:18:24,226
Is the Pegasus really there?

205
00:18:25,264 --> 00:18:27,379
Alright, I'll go, guide the way!

206
00:18:44,539 --> 00:18:46,060
Alright, I have no more use for you!

207
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:47,980
He's here!

208
00:18:48,260 --> 00:18:49,260
He's here!

209
00:18:49,300 --> 00:18:50,300
He's coming, he's coming!

210
00:18:54,860 --> 00:18:55,860
Help!

211
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,180
I'm a friend!

212
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:59,040
Help!

213
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:01,420
I'm a friend!

214
00:19:01,421 --> 00:19:01,655
Help!

215
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:01,680
I'm a friend!

216
00:19:01,681 --> 00:19:01,940
Help!

217
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:02,940
I'm a friend!

218
00:19:05,366 --> 00:19:05,920
You fool!

219
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:07,160
That isn't Sapphire!

220
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:08,246
It IS Sapphire!

221
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:08,895
No!

222
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:10,000
It's not Sapphire!

223
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:12,300
It IS Sapphire!

224
00:19:14,649 --> 00:19:16,033
Ready, fire!

225
00:19:24,109 --> 00:19:25,686
Pegasus, I've come to help!

226
00:19:31,975 --> 00:19:33,173
Sapphire!

227
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:34,300
Tink!

228
00:19:35,179 --> 00:19:35,740
Watch out!

229
00:20:12,049 --> 00:20:16,000
Your Highness, today I shall take your life!

230
00:20:25,889 --> 00:20:27,000
Next is the head!

231
00:20:43,654 --> 00:20:45,966
That was close, Sapphire!

232
00:20:48,329 --> 00:20:49,540
Hey, Pegasus!

233
00:20:50,860 --> 00:20:51,860
Sapphire!

234
00:20:51,899 --> 00:20:53,493
Don't get on that Pegasus!

235
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,086
Wait!

236
00:21:03,110 --> 00:21:05,343
Wait! Mr. Pegasus

237
00:21:10,019 --> 00:21:11,420
Wait!

238
00:21:16,586 --> 00:21:17,402
Tink!

239
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:18,600
Tink!

240
00:21:27,193 --> 00:21:28,713
Help!

241
00:21:31,919 --> 00:21:33,680
It's flying towards the mountain border!

242
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:05,940
Pegasus!

243
00:22:16,044 --> 00:22:17,497
Sapphire!

244
00:22:18,021 --> 00:22:18,768
Tink!

245
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:20,400
Mr. Pegasus!

246
00:22:20,554 --> 00:22:23,060
You mustn't take Sapphire's boy's heart!

247
00:22:24,599 --> 00:22:27,180
Sapphire wants to keep her boy's heart!

248
00:22:27,989 --> 00:22:30,480
This country has so many bad laws!

249
00:22:31,144 --> 00:22:34,140
Until those can be fixed, please leave Sapphire as she is!

250
00:22:35,026 --> 00:22:37,504
If you insist on taking her boy's heart,

251
00:22:37,528 --> 00:22:40,653
I will protect Sapphire even if I have to fight you!

252
00:22:42,729 --> 00:22:48,860
Once Silverland is at peace, I promise I will take her boy's heart back to heaven myself!

253
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:55,280
Mr. Pegasus!

254
00:22:55,495 --> 00:22:57,060
You finally understand!

255
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:01,200
Mr. Pegasus

256
00:23:02,059 --> 00:23:04,440
Give my regards to God in heaven!

257
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:25,246
Pegasus is

258
00:23:25,270 --> 00:23:27,233
going back to heaven!

259
00:23:27,745 --> 00:23:28,745
Goodbye!

260
00:23:28,789 --> 00:23:30,320
Mr. Pegasus!

261
00:23:49,169 --> 00:23:51,699
Happiness isn't brought by Pegasus—

262
00:23:51,723 --> 00:23:53,973
it's something I create with my own power!

263
00:23:54,672 --> 00:23:56,380
Alright, let me do this!

264
00:23:56,794 --> 00:24:01,380
And let me make Silverland an even richer and happier country!

265
00:24:01,404 --> 00:24:03,404

